## 8. Size risk findings

All 11 large files parse cleanly and quickly (whole set fully parsed in one pass); **no file is malformed, truncated, or un-loadable**. Dominance analysis (compact-JSON byte attribution):

| File | Bytes | Compact | Indent overhead | Dominant container | Dominant leaf key (share of that container) |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| #1 parity-inputs | 8,205,267 | 8,202,974 | 0.0% | `datasets` (7,783,037 B = **94.9%**) | **`dataText` = 5,768,523 B (32.9% of `datasets`; 70.3% of the whole file)** |
| #7 oracle | 5,938,727 | 3,103,986 | 47.7% | `observations` (2,638,381 B = 85.0%) | `expected` = 1,769,872 B (20.9% of `observations`) |
| #3 rxa | 767,826 | 554,337 | 27.8% | `triples` (209,969 B = 37.9%) | `inputOccurrences` = 114,760 B (24.2% of `triples`) |
| #12 contracts fixtures | 472,098 | 330,151 | 30.1% | `cases` (181,723 B = 55.1%) | `value` = 154,162 B (43.2%) |
| #8 budget-gaps | 362,492 | 304,523 | 16.0% | `items` (276,881 B = 90.9%) | `missingInvoiceOperations` = 141,860 B (32.6%) |
| #18 tracked-tree | 284,817 | 222,484 | 21.9% | `files` (222,174 B = 99.9%) | `path` = 86,721 B (53.8%) |
| #4 product-cases | 188,023 | 123,122 | 34.5% | `cases` (100%) | `expected` = 75,479 B (26.3%) |
| #9 coverage | 154,032 | 114,323 | 25.8% | `pending` (98,113 B = 85.9%) | `fields` = 91,811 B (49.7%) |
| #14 binding-regressions | 123,964 | 85,998 | 30.6% | `cases` (99.9%) | `value` = 72,163 B (31.5%) |
| #13 contracts schema | 122,889 | 60,795 | 50.5% | `$defs` (99.8%) | `oneOf` = 45,757 B (22.2%) |
| #11 sources | 79,253 | 64,419 | 18.7% | `inputOriginLineage` (60.3%) | `record` = 25,653 B (44.9%) |

**Risk assessment against AGENTS.md "don't commit large raw data":**
- **File #1 is the material risk**: 5.77 MB of the 8.21 MB is a single repeated field, `datasets[*].dataText` — raw Turtle/Shacl source text for 320 datasets. It is *committed* raw data. Note `sources.json` labels this file `"sealed pure input, not expected"`, so it is deliberate sealed input rather than accidental dump — but it is the largest committed artifact in the scope.
- **Files #7 and #13 carry substantial formatting overhead**: 47.7% and 50.5% of their bytes are pure indentation (the oracle is pretty-printed to 178,575 lines; the contracts schema to 4,752 lines). Recompacting would cut ~3.48 MB across the two with zero content change — but note the repo may rely on line-addressable diffs, so this is an observation, not a recommendation.
- **File #2 is single-line JSON** (1 line, 8.2 MB) — the opposite extreme, which makes any line-level diff of #1 unreviewable.
- No file contains base64 blobs, embedded binaries, or duplicated copies of the same payload beyond the documented `rawTermSourceOccurrences`/source-record duplication (verified byte-equal, so it is redundancy by design: 25 arrays reproduce their input records verbatim).

